WEBVTT

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.428
Every bitcoin in existence
sits in an unspent output.

00:00:04.428 --> 00:00:08.348
Every one of those outputs
is here, in this landscape.

00:00:08.348 --> 00:00:10.708
Let's learn to read it.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.376
From above, it becomes a map.

00:00:17.376 --> 00:00:23.943
Time runs left to right, from the first
block in 2009 to the newest, at the right.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:26.779
Amount runs upward:

00:00:26.779 --> 00:00:32.286
dust at the bottom, whole coins
in the middle, whales at the top.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.736
Every dot on this map is a cell.

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:38.596
We'll come back to one.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:41.503
Seventeen years of blocks, sampled.

00:00:41.503 --> 00:00:47.371
The field only grows at its
right-hand edge, one block at a time.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:51.308
The oldest row still standing:

00:00:51.308 --> 00:00:56.825
about fifty bitcoin each, the
block reward of 2009 and 2010.

00:00:56.825 --> 00:01:00.234
Thirty-three thousand
of them, never moved.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.984
Bright lines are popular amounts:

00:01:02.984 --> 00:01:06.721
a hundredth, a tenth, one whole bitcoin.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.013
Then, from 2023, a ridge of tiny outputs:

00:01:12.013 --> 00:01:15.924
a few hundred satoshis each, piled high.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:17.920
And here:

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:22.519
one cell with thirty-five outputs
of exactly one thousand bitcoin,

00:01:22.519 --> 00:01:24.758
made within ten hours.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:27.100
This is the newest edge.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.244
Now, one cell:

00:01:31.244 --> 00:01:34.145
everything made in the
same sixty-four blocks,

00:01:34.145 --> 00:01:38.150
about half a day, at
nearly the same amount.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:42.190
This one holds 214 outputs
of about one bitcoin.

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:44.407
Each division is one output;

00:01:44.407 --> 00:01:46.950
the height is the count.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.143
Now let eight days of real blocks run.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:55.944
Seventeen outputs, spent
in a single block.

00:01:55.944 --> 00:01:59.382
Spent outputs leave the unspent set.

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:02.378
The same eight days, from above.

00:02:02.378 --> 00:02:04.692
Every flash is a spend:

00:02:04.692 --> 00:02:08.333
old coins waking up
across seventeen years.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:13.860
Here they are again, in
the original film's look.

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.080
The chain breathes:

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:18.327
in at the edge, out from everywhere.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:21.792
Colour can answer different questions.

00:02:21.792 --> 00:02:25.700
Here, the warmer the
colour, the more outputs.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:30.112
And here, the warmer the
colour, the more bitcoin.

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:36.477
Fewer than two outputs in a thousand hold
eighty-four percent of all the bitcoin.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.449
The same data, in eleven looks:

00:02:39.449 --> 00:02:42.297
some for beauty, some for measuring.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:56.344
Change the shape of a cell, how tall the
big coins stand, or the time of day.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:04.623
Twelve hundred blocks later, our
column holds ninety-four outputs.

00:03:04.623 --> 00:03:06.750
This is what remains.

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:11.226
Explore it yourself, at
bitcoinlandscape.com.
